msgstr "2026-04-21"

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:11
msgid "landlock_create_ruleset - create a new Landlock ruleset"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:19
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"B<#include E<lt>linux/landlock.hE<gt>>  /* Definition of B<LANDLOCK_*> constants */\n"
"B<#include E<lt>sys/syscall.hE<gt>>     /* Definition of B<SYS_*> constants */\n"
"B<#include E<lt>unistd.hE<gt>>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:23
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"B<int syscall(SYS_landlock_create_ruleset,>\n"
"B<            const struct landlock_ruleset_attr *>I<attr>B<,>\n"
"B<            size_t >I<size>B< , uint32_t >I<flags>B<);>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:37
msgid ""
"A Landlock ruleset identifies a set of rules (i.e., actions on objects).  "
"This B<landlock_create_ruleset>()  system call creates a new file descriptor "
"which identifies a ruleset.  This file descriptor can then be used by "
"B<landlock_add_rule>(2)  and B<landlock_restrict_self>(2).  See "
"B<landlock>(7)  for a global overview."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:41
msgid ""
"I<attr> specifies the properties of the new ruleset.  It points to the "
"following structure:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:49
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"struct landlock_ruleset_attr {\n"
"    __u64 handled_access_fs;\n"
"    __u64 handled_access_net;\n"
"    __u64 scoped;\n"
"};\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:58
msgid ""
"I<handled_access_fs> is a bitmask of handled filesystem actions (see "
"B<Filesystem actions> in B<landlock>(7))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:65
msgid ""
"I<handled_access_net> is a bitmask of handled network actions (see B<Network "
"actions> in B<landlock>(7))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:72
msgid ""
"I<scoped> is a bitmask of scope flags (see B<Scope flags> in B<landlock>(7))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:81
msgid ""
"This structure defines a set of I<handled access rights>, a set of actions "
"on different object types, which should be denied by default when the "
"ruleset is enacted.  Vice versa, access rights that are not specifically "
"listed here are not going to be denied by this ruleset when it is enacted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:93
msgid ""
"For historical reasons, the B<LANDLOCK_ACCESS_FS_REFER> right is always "
"denied by default, even when its bit is not set in I<handled_access_fs>.  In "
"order to add new rules with this access right, the bit must still be set "
"explicitly (see B<Filesystem actions> in B<landlock>(7))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:102
msgid ""
"The explicit listing of I<handled access rights> is required for backwards "
"compatibility reasons.  In most use cases, processes that use Landlock will "
"I<handle> a wide range or all access rights that they know about at build "
"time (and that they have tested with a kernel that supported them all)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:104
msgid "This structure can grow in future Landlock versions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:109
msgid ""
"I<size> must be specified as I<sizeof(struct landlock_ruleset_attr)> for "
"compatibility reasons."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:117
msgid ""
"I<flags> must be 0 if I<attr> is used.  Otherwise, I<flags> can be set to:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:117
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<LANDLOCK_CREATE_RULESET_VERSION>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:124
msgid ""
"Return the highest supported Landlock ABI version (starting at 1).  This "
"version can be used for a best-effort security approach, which is encouraged "
"when user space is not pinned to a specific kernel version."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:128
msgid ""
"Unless noted otherwise, all features documented in these manual pages are "
"available with the version 1."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:128
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<LANDLOCK_CREATE_RULESET_ERRATA>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:135
msgid ""
"Return a bitmask of fixed issues for the current Landlock ABI version.  If "
"bit N is set (i.e., I<errata\\~&\\~(1\\~E<lt>E<lt>\\~(N\\~-\\~1))>), then "
"erratum N has been fixed in the running kernel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:141
msgid ""
"In addition to ABI versions, Landlock's errata mechanism tracks fixes for "
"issues that may affect backwards compatibility or require userspace "
"awareness."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:144
msgid ""
"Only check errata if your application specifically relies on behavior that "
"changed due to the fix."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:148
msgid ""
"The full list of Landlock errata is available at E<.UR https:\\://docs."
"kernel.org/\\:userspace-api/\\:landlock.html#landlock-errata> E<.UE .>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:155
msgid ""
"This flag is available on all Linux versions where Landlock errata were "
"fixed.  This specifically includes all newest bugfix releases of stable "
"kernels where Landlock is supported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:166
msgid ""
"If B<LANDLOCK_CREATE_RULESET_VERSION> or B<LANDLOCK_CREATE_RULESET_ERRATA> "
"is set, then I<attr> must be NULL and I<size> must be 0."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:174
msgid ""
"On success, B<landlock_create_ruleset>()  returns a new Landlock ruleset "
"file descriptor, a Landlock ABI version, or a Landlock errata bitmask, "
"according to I<flags>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/landlock_create_ruleset.2:179
#: build/C/man2/process_madvise.2:138 build/C/man2/process_vm_readv.2:207
